# KEYMAP.md §Dialogs and text inputs — Help (`?`): "`Esc` / `?` close", `ctrl-tab` switches the
# tab, `↑`/`↓` move, `⏎` runs; UX-SPEC §3.8.7 — Help is a guide, and every row runs.
#
# Help is the discoverability promise of a modal app, and it is the one dialog with two ways
# out. Both are checked, because `?` closing is the half a refactor drops: `?` is still bound
# under `Hub`, and a Help overlay that does not bind it for itself simply re-opens.
#
# Then the guide itself, by pointer only: a new user opens Help, picks "Start work on a task"
# and clicks its first step's button, which closes Help and runs `g b` on the Hub behind it.
fixture: one-repo
await idle 30000
assert screen == Hub && overlay absent

key ?
await overlay == Dialog 10000
assert mode == Dialog && dialog.name == Help
assert key_contexts[0] == Dialog && key_contexts[1] == Help
# It opens on the Guides tab: a search field, the six things the Worktrees list is for, and
# the guides, with the first one shown.
await targets["help.search"] exists 10000
assert targets["help.tab[0]"] exists && targets["help.tab[1]"] exists
assert targets["help.here[0]"] exists && targets["help.here[5]"] exists
assert targets["help.guide[0]"] exists && targets["help.guide[6]"] exists
assert targets["help.step[0].action[0]"] exists
assert dialog.fields[0].name == search && dialog.fields[0].focused == true
shot help
dump help

# `?` closes it ...
key ?
await overlay absent
assert screen == Hub && mode == Normal && focused == worktrees.row[0]

# ... and so does `Esc`, from the same place.
key ?
await overlay == Dialog 10000
assert dialog.name == Help
key escape
await overlay absent
assert screen == Hub && mode == Normal && dialog absent
dump closed

# A guide by pointer: the list shows it, and its steps each carry a button with its key.
key ?
await overlay == Dialog 10000
await targets["help.guide[4]"] exists 10000
click help.guide[4]
await targets["help.step[5].action[0]"] exists 5000
shot help-automate-guide

# `↓` and `↑` walk the list the field sits over; typing goes to the field.
key down
key up
type agent
await dialog.fields[0].value == agent 5000
await targets["help.shortcut[0]"] exists 5000
shot help-search-guides

# All shortcuts, by the tab switch: the table searches the same query, grouped by where it works.
click help.tab[1]
await targets["help.place[0]"] exists 5000
await targets["help.shortcut[0]"] exists 5000
assert dialog.fields[0].value == agent
shot help-shortcuts-agent

# `ctrl-tab` goes back, keeping the query.
key ctrl-tab
await targets["help.guide[1]"] exists 5000
key escape
await overlay absent
assert screen == Hub && mode == Normal

# The footer's Run doctor closes Help and raises the doctor report, which replaces the Hub's
# body until `Esc` dismisses it. The report has no snapshot field of its own, so the worktree
# row it covers is the observable.
key ?
await overlay == Dialog 10000
await targets["dialog.button[0]"] exists 10000
click dialog.button[0]
await overlay absent 10000
await targets["worktrees.row[0]"] absent 30000
shot help-ran-doctor
key escape
await targets["worktrees.row[0]"] exists 10000

# A new user completes the first step of "Start work on a task" by clicking only.
key ?
await overlay == Dialog 10000
await targets["help.guide[0]"] exists 10000
click help.guide[0]
await targets["help.step[0].action[0]"] exists 5000
click help.step[0].action[0]
await overlay absent 10000
await hub_tab == Board 10000
assert screen == Hub && dialog absent
shot help-ran-go-to-board
quit
